  "label": "Canadian Firearms Policy",
  "description": "Refers to the legal and regulatory framework governing firearms in Canada, including the requirement for background checks, licensing, and the prohibition of certain types of weapons. The meme references this policy to create a false equivalence by suggesting that if Syrian migrants are not trusted, then even 'safest demographics' in Canada should have their firearms taken away. This requires knowledge of Canadian gun laws and the political debates surrounding them, which are not visible in the image.",
